# Then modify configure.wrf by commenting out the existing DEP_LIB_PATH variable definition and
add the new definition shown below. 
This makes sure that the correct hdf library path and mkl library path are defined. The library mkl is intel math library required by 3DPBL for solving systems of linear equations using LU decomposition (based on LAPACK library).

#DEP_LIB_PATH    = -L/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/netcdf-fortran-4.6.0-2ptt3qnjy5vtg5s4fvo7l5qyjomufnrt/lib

DEP_LIB_PATH    = -L/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/netcdf-c-4.9.2-twcnffnqrckvlwqn7udxatwmyf26r6es/lib -lnetcdf -L/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/netcdf-fortran-4.6.0-2ptt3qnjy5vtg5s4fvo7l5qyjomufnrt/lib -lnetcdff -lnetcdf -lnetcdf -lm 

Add the following line under definition of LIB_BUNDLED as follows:

LIB_MKL         = -L/nopt/nrel/apps/libraries/08-23/spack/opt/spack/linux-rhel8-icelake/intel-2021.10.0/hdf5-1.14.1-2-x43jlkan4ddpbd3hq7rzntsdmrq4qery/lib -L/nopt/nrel/apps/cpu_stack/libraries-intel/06-24/linux-rhel8-sapphirerapids/oneapi-2024.1.0/intel-oneapi-mkl-2023.2.0-cxkmsrntwshafhfoubnmiimvx6mn7ofl/lib/intel64 -Wl,--no-as-needed -lmkl_intel_lp64 -lmkl_sequential -lmkl_core -lm

